            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Mandarin for to keep the New Year vigil, then the Mandarin for to pay a New Year call."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 正月",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "正月 — zhēngyuè — \"first lunar month\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "正月里大家都很开心 zhēngyuè lǐ dàjiā dōu hěn kāixīn — In the first month everyone is cheerful."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "正 is said zhēng here, with a level tone, not the zhèng of 正在."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "正月 (zhēngyuè) is built from 正 and 月 'a month', both inherited from Middle Chinese, tsyeng and ngjwot (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription). The dictionary gives the first its level-tone reading tsyeng for the start of the calendar year, apart from tsyengH, 'upright': so zhēng here, and zhèng in 正在."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
