          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 红包",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "红包 — hóngbāo — \"red envelope\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "过年的时候外公给了我一个红包 guònián de shíhou wàigōng gěi le wǒ yí ge hóngbāo — At the new year my grandpa gave me a red envelope."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The new character, in pieces: 红 (hóng) — six strokes: on the left the silk piece of 给, three strokes; on the right 工. The next lesson puts it in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "红包 (hóngbāo) is built from 红 (hóng) 'red' and 包 'a packet', both inherited from Middle Chinese, huwng and paew (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'a colour' and the second 'to wrap'."
            }
          ]
